## iced_dock

The docking layout implementation under `src/dock/` is a port of
[`iced_dock`](https://github.com/Fee0/iced_dock), by Fee0.

- **Licence:** MIT (declared in the upstream `Cargo.toml`; the upstream
  repository does not ship a standalone `LICENSE` file)
- **What was ported:** the complete `src/` tree — 24 files, ~8,700 lines —
  covering the layout model, builder, dock widget, tab strip, split container,
  manager, factory and styling types.
- **What was changed:**
  - Import paths, so the code resolves inside this crate (`crate::x` becomes
    `crate::dock::x`).
  - The `serde` feature is renamed `dock-serde`, and the required
    `slotmap/serde` dependency is declared.
  - Doc comments that referred to the crate by name now refer to this module.
  - The tab strip's bundled SVG assets moved to `assets/` at the repository
    root, with the `include_bytes!` paths updated.

  The layout algorithm, widget behaviour, event model and styling structure are
  upstream's work.

## Design language

The token names and values, and the component vocabulary, follow these
projects. Nothing is copied verbatim, but the provenance is stated here for
clarity:

| Source | Licence | What came from it |
| --- | --- | --- |
| [gpui-kit](https://github.com/longbridge/gpui-kit) | Apache-2.0 | Semantic token names and values, component naming |
| [shadcn/ui](https://ui.shadcn.com/) | MIT | The semantic token vocabulary |
| [iced-astraui](https://github.com/AstraBrew-Labs/iced-astraui) | MIT | Implementation patterns (design tokens, global layers) |
| [shadcn-rs](https://github.com/FerrisMind/shadcn-rs) | MIT / Apache-2.0 | Implementation patterns (data table, charts) |

## iced

This crate builds on [`iced`](https://github.com/iced-rs/iced), which is
licensed MIT. It is used as an ordinary dependency and is not vendored.

## Lucide icons

The icons are drawn from the [Lucide](https://lucide.dev) icon set, used through
[`lucide-icons`](https://github.com/WhySoBad/lucide-icons-rs), an ordinary
dependency that bundles the font.

- **Licence:** MIT AND ISC (the icon set is ISC; the Rust wrapper is MIT)
- **What is used:** the bundled `lucide.ttf`, its `Icon` enum (re-exported here
  as `IconName`), and the font bytes re-exported as `LUCIDE_FONT_BYTES`.

The settings component's structure — pages holding groups, groups holding
labelled items, and the render options threaded through them — follows
`gpui-kit`'s `setting` module, as noted under the design language above.
